DESCRIPTION                   = "This is a P2 revision of label file
 CMB_776288153MIN42661080792CH00113P1. The label for the P1 version
 had reported amorphous and clay mineral values with a single percentage 
 value of ~58 weight%. The P2 revision provides separate percentages for
 these constituents. This change affects only the DESCRIPTION section in
 the label; entries tabulated in the original csv file remain unchanged.
 The table contains mineral abundances and analytical errors derived from
 diffraction-all K-alpha diffraction data for the Kings Canyon drill
 sample, analyzed in CheMin cell number 2b (Kapton window). The analysis
 is based on RDA file  CMB_776288153RDA42661080792CH00113P1. Mineral
 identifications, abundances and analytical errors for crystalline phases
 were determined using the program JADE. The Fe-Mg-Ca carbonate abundance
 was estimated by fitting both ankerite and dolomite to the pattern, without
 refining their cell parameters. In addition to these crystalline phases,
 the program FULLPAT was used to estimate the abundance of poorly crystalline
 clay minerals at ~7 +/- 3 weight% of the total sample. High intensity in the
 low 2-theta region and a broad amorphous hump were modeled using FULLPAT to
 indicate that ~51 +/- 25 weight% of the total sample consists of X-ray
 amorphous materials. All errors cited are 2-sigma. Column 1 of the table
 lists mineral identifications, column 2 lists the mineral abundances in
 weight percent, and column 3 indicates the estimated analytical errors."
END_OBJECT                    = SPREADSHEET
END
